WEBVTT

00:00:09.892 --> 00:00:12.061
Harry.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.031
This is mad.
Who'd wanna be taught by me?

00:00:24.198 --> 00:00:25.408
I'm a nutter, remember?

00:00:25.575 --> 00:00:28.969
Look on the bright side: you can't
be any worse than old toad face.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:32.541
-Thanks, Ron.
-I'm here for you, mate.

00:00:34.292 --> 00:00:35.907
Who's supposed to be meeting us, then?

00:00:36.794 --> 00:00:38.471
Just a couple of people.

00:00:43.926 --> 00:00:45.261
Lovely spot.

00:00:49.098 --> 00:00:51.225
Thought it would be safer
off the beaten track.

00:00:51.392 --> 00:00:53.131
Matey, come back here.

00:00:59.609 --> 00:01:00.800
Um....

00:01:01.986 --> 00:01:03.234
Hi.

00:01:03.571 --> 00:01:06.239
So you all know why we're here.

00:01:06.616 --> 00:01:07.867
We need a teacher.

00:01:09.577 --> 00:01:10.846
A proper teacher.

00:01:11.954 --> 00:01:15.124
One who's had experience defending
themselves against the Dark Arts.

00:01:15.291 --> 00:01:16.533
- Why?
- Why?

00:01:17.251 --> 00:01:19.295
Because You-Know-Who's back,
you tosspot.

00:01:19.462 --> 00:01:21.130
- So he says.
- So Dumbledore says.

00:01:21.297 --> 00:01:23.041
So Dumbledore says because he says.

00:01:23.507 --> 00:01:24.925
The point is, where's the proof?

00:01:27.643 --> 00:01:30.306
If Potter could tell us more
about how Diggory got killed....

00:01:33.392 --> 00:01:36.823
I'm not gonna talk about Cedric, so if
that's why you're here, clear out now.

00:01:37.313 --> 00:01:38.481
Come on, Hermione.

00:01:38.648 --> 00:01:40.858
They're here because they think
I'm some sort of freak.

00:01:41.025 --> 00:01:42.923
Is it true you can produce
a Patronus Charm?

00:01:46.989 --> 00:01:48.067
Yes.

00:01:50.157 --> 00:01:51.327
I've seen it.

00:01:51.494 --> 00:01:53.621
Blimey, Harry.
I didn't know you could do that.

00:01:54.288 --> 00:01:58.417
And he killed a basilisk, with the sword
in Dumbledore's office.

00:01:58.484 --> 00:01:59.485
It's true.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.875
Third year, he fought off
about a hundred Dementors at once.

00:02:04.388 --> 00:02:06.632
Last year, he really did fight off
You-Know-Who in the flesh.

00:02:06.699 --> 00:02:07.784
Wait.

00:02:09.011 --> 00:02:13.557
Look, it all sounds great
when you say it like that...

00:02:13.724 --> 00:02:16.291
...but the truth is,
most of that was just luck.

00:02:17.561 --> 00:02:20.255
I didn't know what I was doing
half the time. I nearly always had help.

00:02:21.482 --> 00:02:23.996
-He's just being modest.
-No, Hermione, I'm not.

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:31.531
Facing this stuff in real life
is not like school.

00:02:33.244 --> 00:02:36.446
In school, if you make a mistake,
you can just try again tomorrow.

00:02:36.872 --> 00:02:38.374
But out there...

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:42.253
...when you're a second away
from being murdered...

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:45.132
...or watching a friend die
right before your eyes....

00:02:48.884 --> 00:02:50.080
You don't know what that's like.

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:01.414
You're right, Harry, we don't.

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:04.394
That's why we need your help.

00:03:05.401 --> 00:03:07.230
Because if we're going to have
any chance at beating...

00:03:10.531 --> 00:03:11.699
...Voldemort....

00:03:15.119 --> 00:03:16.241
He's really back?

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.018
Right.

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:40.644
First we need to find
a place to practice...

00:03:40.811 --> 00:03:42.438
...where Umbridge won't find out.

00:03:42.515 --> 00:03:44.494
-The Shrieking Shack.
-It's too small.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:47.352
-Forbidden Forest?
-Not b***dy likely.

00:03:47.549 --> 00:03:50.154
Harry, what happens
if Umbridge does find out?

00:03:50.321 --> 00:03:51.489
Who cares?

00:03:52.114 --> 00:03:56.282
I mean, it's sort of exciting, isn't it,
breaking the rules?

00:03:57.119 --> 00:03:59.093
Who are you and what have you done
with Hermione?

00:04:00.122 --> 00:04:03.173
Anyway, at least we know
one positive thing that came from today.

00:04:03.959 --> 00:04:05.252
What's that?

00:04:06.962 --> 00:04:09.032
Cho couldn't take her eyes off you,
could she?

00:04:12.384 --> 00:04:15.471
Right. Over the next few days,
we should each come up...

00:04:15.638 --> 00:04:18.024
...with a couple of possibilities
of places we can practice.

00:04:18.641 --> 00:04:22.478
We've got to make sure, wherever it is,
there's no chance she can find us.

00:04:22.645 --> 00:04:24.480
Will do, Harry.

00:04:33.155 --> 00:04:37.284
All student organizations
are henceforth disbanded.

00:04:37.493 --> 00:04:40.079
Any student in noncompliance
will be expelled.

00:04:41.237 --> 00:04:43.249
Watch where you're going, Longbottom.

00:05:19.451 --> 00:05:22.696
You've done it, Neville.
You found the Room of Requirement.

00:05:23.873 --> 00:05:24.999
The what?

00:05:25.166 --> 00:05:26.925
It's also known as
the Come and Go Room.

00:05:27.751 --> 00:05:30.532
The Room of Requirement only appears
when a person has real need of it.

00:05:31.338 --> 00:05:33.488
And it's always equipped
for the seeker's needs.

00:05:34.175 --> 00:05:36.858
So say you really needed the toilet....

00:05:39.096 --> 00:05:43.934
Charming, Ronald.
But, yes, that is the general idea.

00:05:44.101 --> 00:05:47.831
It's brilliant. It's like Hogwarts
wants us to fight back.

00:06:00.075 --> 00:06:01.577
Expelliarmus.

00:06:02.077 --> 00:06:03.370
Whoa!

00:06:06.665 --> 00:06:08.042
I'm hopeless.

00:06:08.209 --> 00:06:12.004
You're just flourishing your wand
too much. Try it like this. Expelliarmus.

00:06:15.382 --> 00:06:19.386
You will please copy
the approved text four times...

00:06:19.595 --> 00:06:22.598
...to ensure maximum retention.

00:06:22.932 --> 00:06:26.644
-There will be no need to talk.
-No need to think's more like it.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:29.647
- Expelliarmus.
- Wands away.

00:06:41.784 --> 00:06:44.870
Stunning is one of the most useful spells
in your arsenal.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:47.248
It's a wizard's bread and butter, really.

00:06:47.414 --> 00:06:51.001
So, um, come on, then, Nigel.
Give it your best shot.

00:06:57.508 --> 00:06:58.926
Stupefy!

00:07:03.806 --> 00:07:07.189
Good. Not bad at all, Nigel. Well done.

00:07:13.649 --> 00:07:15.734
Don't worry. I'll go easy on you.

00:07:16.151 --> 00:07:18.153
Thanks, Ronald.

00:07:20.781 --> 00:07:22.950
- Come on, Ron.
- Come on, Ron.

00:07:23.158 --> 00:07:25.995
- You can do it.
- Come on, Ron.

00:07:26.537 --> 00:07:28.580
-One Sickle.
-You're on.

00:07:35.671 --> 00:07:36.672
Stupefy.

00:07:42.678 --> 00:07:44.680
-Thank you.
-Shut up.

00:07:45.014 --> 00:07:49.685
I let her do that.
It's good manners, isn't it?

00:07:51.854 --> 00:07:54.398
It was completely intentional.

